WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:07.941
In this video, you will see how many people found your contest: page visits, visits from your QR code, and votes, day by day.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:10.574
That tells you which kind of sharing works.

00:00:10.574 --> 00:00:11.771
We start on the map.

00:00:12.671 --> 00:00:16.733
To begin, open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:16.733 --> 00:00:18.858
That is the only address you need.

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.322
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:26.415
The first time you visit, it asks to use your location.

00:00:26.415 --> 00:00:27.520
Tap Use my location.

00:00:29.641 --> 00:00:32.364
That is how the map shows how far things are, and gives you directions.

00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:34.331
Your browser asks permission as well, so tap Allow.

00:00:34.331 --> 00:00:37.129
Your location is used only on your device, and you can say no at any time.

00:00:40.262 --> 00:00:42.951
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:42.951 --> 00:00:44.147
See the three dots?

00:00:44.147 --> 00:00:48.449
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:48.987
Tap them.

00:00:50.818 --> 00:00:52.456
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:52.456 --> 00:00:57.794
That is where every neighborhood contest lives: the ones you can vote in, enter, or run.

00:00:59.531 --> 00:01:00.113
Tap Mine.

00:01:00.113 --> 00:01:01.745
This is your personal page.

00:01:01.745 --> 00:01:07.104
It lists the contests you run, if you run any, and the homes you entered, with their status.

00:01:08.827 --> 00:01:10.873
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:01:10.873 --> 00:01:14.545
This opens your dashboard, the control room for your contest.

00:01:16.459 --> 00:01:18.743
Want to know whether your sharing is working?

00:01:18.743 --> 00:01:19.339
Tap Promote.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:30.088
Activity shows three numbers: how many people have visited your contest page, how many arrived by scanning your QR code, and how many people have voted.

00:01:30.988 --> 00:01:33.700
Below, a chart shows the votes for each day.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:36.171
Use it to see which sharing worked best.

00:01:36.171 --> 00:01:40.993
If votes jump the day after a flyer went up, or after an email, do more of that.

00:01:41.895 --> 00:01:44.220
Next up: Add sponsors and logos.
